/**
 * # Bounty hunting: how a criminal looks
 *
 * Owner: P1 identity. Do not edit this file outside P1.
 *
 * What it owns: the look builder that puts the same face (a /datum/bounty_look) on any mob in any
 * outfit, for any species in the pool, cached per record and outfit; and the mugshot, built once
 * per record, served to the UI as an asset (spec sections 2, 8 and 10). Mugshots never go through
 * a ui_data() payload.
 *
 * The shared vars are declared in bounty_types.dm and nowhere else; a var only P1 uses goes here
 * with an `identity_` prefix. The procs below start as P0 stubs.
 */

/**
 * Dresses `target` as the person in `record` wearing `outfit`: the same face in any outfit. Can
 * sleep, so call it from an async proc.
 *
 * P0 stub: an ordinary outpost NPC look in the outfit, for the record's gender.
 */
/proc/apply_bounty_look(mob/living/target, datum/bounty_record/record, outfit)
	set_outpost_npc_look(target, outfit, record?.gender, 1)

/// Their mugshot as a base64 PNG, built once and cached on the record. P0 stub: none ("").
/proc/bounty_record_mugshot(datum/bounty_record/record)
	return ""

/// The name of the asset the UI loads the mugshot from (through ui_static_data() or an asset), never sent in ui_data(). P0 stub: none ("").
/proc/bounty_mugshot_asset(datum/bounty_record/record)
	return ""
